	(text "Soft power latch, all JLC Basic parts. Q101/Q102 hold 3V3_EN on without firmware; SW101 sets it through R105/D101.\nOff: firmware drives PWR_OFF high (Q103), or the button is held 6-9 s (R108/C104 charge until Q104 conducts).\nFirmware: PWR_BTN is low while the button is pressed. Before driving PWR_OFF, WAIT FOR THE BUTTON TO BE RELEASED,\nor the held button re-latches the rail when 3V3 collapses. Keep PWR_OFF high until power is gone.\nC101 keeps Q101 off on VSYS steps (cell inserted, USB plugged). Verified in ngspice over 48 corners (Vth, hFE, 3.0-4.2 V, leakage).\nUSB plug-in turns it on: the VBUS edge through C105 sets K via D103/R110 (~0.5 s pulse, R109 bleeds C105), so the\nfirmware can raise the charge current. Only the edge: switched off while plugged in, it stays off. Simulated in ngspice:\nlatches with VSYS 3.0-4.2 V, VBUS ramps up to 100 ms, and a dead cell when VSYS comes up to 350 ms after VBUS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 71.12 127 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "faccdf49-b228-4ba5-9f95-27d12c27cd5e")
	)
